<Legal
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Simon Maps and its geospatial software tools collect, use, and protect information."
  path="/privacy"
  updated="18 October 2026"
>
  <p>This policy explains how Simon Maps ("Simon Maps", "we", "us"), operated by Simon Mutunga in Nairobi, Kenya, handles information on www.simonmapper.co.ke and in the software tools published under the simonmapper.co.ke domain.</p>

  <h2>Who our software is for</h2>
  <p>Most Simon Maps software is built to assist Simon Mutunga and scientific colleagues with geospatial tasks such as processing spatial data, analysing satellite imagery, and mapping climate and environmental risk. Some tools are also shared publicly as demonstrations.</p>

  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>This website:</strong> no account is needed and no forms store your details. When you contact us by WhatsApp, phone, or email, we receive what you choose to send.</li>
    <li><strong>Sign-in:</strong> if a tool asks you to sign in (for example with a Google account), we receive only basic profile details such as your name, email address, and profile picture, used to identify you within that tool.</li>
    <li><strong>Data you provide:</strong> files, coordinates, or datasets you upload to a tool are used only to perform the task you request.</li>
    <li><strong>Technical data:</strong> our hosting provider may log standard request data such as IP address, browser type, and pages visited, for security and reliability.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we use information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To provide, operate, and improve the tools and services you use.</li>
    <li>To respond to enquiries and deliver requested services.</li>
    <li>To keep our services secure and prevent misuse.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell personal information, do not use it for advertising, and do not share it with third parties except the service providers needed to run our tools (such as hosting) or where required by law.</p>

  <h2>Google user data</h2>
  <p>Where a Simon Maps tool uses Google sign-in or Google APIs, its use of information received from Google APIs adheres to the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including the Limited Use requirements. Google user data is used only to provide the features you request and is not transferred, sold, or used for advertising.</p>

  <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
  <p>We keep information only as long as needed for the purpose it was collected. You can ask us to delete your account data or any data you have provided at any time by emailing <a href="mailto:besimonmutunga@gmail.com">besimonmutunga@gmail.com</a>. You can also revoke a tool's access to your Google account at <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">myaccount.google.com/permissions</a>.</p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>Data is transmitted over encrypted connections (HTTPS) and access is limited to what is needed to operate each tool.</p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>Our services are intended for professional and research use and are not directed at children under 13.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy from time to time. The date at the top of this page shows when it last changed.</p>

